1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,728
Rub your palms fast, and they warm up.

2
00:00:02,728 --> 00:00:05,264
Pump a bicycle tyre,
and the pump gets hot.

3
00:00:05,264 --> 00:00:08,009
Steam in a pressure cooker
lifts the heavy weight.

4
00:00:08,409 --> 00:00:09,937
Work turns into heat.

5
00:00:09,937 --> 00:00:11,465
Heat turns into work.

6
00:00:11,465 --> 00:00:13,400
One rule keeps the accounts.

7
00:00:13,850 --> 00:00:16,884
Aarav is pumping his
bicycle tyre before college.

8
00:00:17,234 --> 00:00:18,330
Ten quick pushes.

9
00:00:18,330 --> 00:00:19,606
He touches the pump.

10
00:00:19,606 --> 00:00:20,506
It is warm.

11
00:00:20,445 --> 00:00:21,943
But no flame touched it.

12
00:00:22,443 --> 00:00:25,670
By the end, you will know
where that warmth came from.

13
00:00:25,670 --> 00:00:27,905
It is the First Law of Thermodynamics.

14
00:00:28,555 --> 00:00:31,313
Every system has energy stored inside it.

15
00:00:31,313 --> 00:00:34,040
Think of it as a piggy bank of energy.

16
00:00:34,390 --> 00:00:36,466
Its molecules move, spin and shake.

17
00:00:36,466 --> 00:00:38,112
Their bonds hold energy too.

18
00:00:38,512 --> 00:00:41,930
All of this together is
the internal energy, U.

19
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:45,226
We cannot count all the coins in the bank.

20
00:00:45,226 --> 00:00:47,801
We only measure the change, delta U.

21
00:00:48,201 --> 00:00:49,696
U is a state function.

22
00:00:49,696 --> 00:00:52,550
Delta U depends only on
the start and the end.

23
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:58,331
Now a gas in a cylinder, with a
piston on top, on our molecule bench.

24
00:00:58,681 --> 00:01:00,780
Way one to fill the bank: work.

25
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:02,173
Push the piston down.

26
00:01:02,173 --> 00:01:05,430
The molecules bounce off a
moving wall, and speed up.

27
00:01:05,830 --> 00:01:07,714
Faster molecules, higher temperature.

28
00:01:07,714 --> 00:01:08,614
U goes up.

29
00:01:08,432 --> 00:01:09,822
That is Aarav's warm pump.

30
00:01:10,222 --> 00:01:11,213
Way two: heat.

31
00:01:11,213 --> 00:01:12,952
Put a flame under the cylinder.

32
00:01:12,952 --> 00:01:15,602
Heat flows in, and again
the molecules speed up.

33
00:01:16,002 --> 00:01:18,397
Now let the gas push the piston up.

34
00:01:18,397 --> 00:01:20,878
The gas does work on the surroundings.

35
00:01:20,878 --> 00:01:23,215
It spends energy, so U goes down.

36
00:01:23,615 --> 00:01:27,341
So energy crosses the
boundary in only two ways.

37
00:01:27,341 --> 00:01:30,050
As heat, q, and as work, w.

38
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:31,801
Now the signs.

39
00:01:31,801 --> 00:01:34,803
Stand inside the system,
and watch your bank.

40
00:01:35,153 --> 00:01:38,044
Heat flowing in, from the
surroundings, is plus.

41
00:01:38,044 --> 00:01:39,651
Heat flowing out is minus.

42
00:01:40,051 --> 00:01:42,345
Work done on the system is plus.

43
00:01:42,345 --> 00:01:44,689
Work done by the system is minus.

44
00:01:45,089 --> 00:01:46,329
Just like money.

45
00:01:46,329 --> 00:01:49,031
Money in is plus, money out is minus.

46
00:01:49,431 --> 00:01:50,497
Add them up.

47
00:01:50,497 --> 00:01:52,371
Delta U equals q plus w.

48
00:01:52,371 --> 00:01:55,136
This is the First Law of Thermodynamics.

49
00:01:55,786 --> 00:01:58,630
In words, energy can neither
be made nor destroyed.

50
00:01:58,630 --> 00:01:59,903
It only changes form.

51
00:02:00,253 --> 00:02:03,611
So the energy of an isolated
system stays constant.

52
00:02:04,011 --> 00:02:05,279
Pause and think.

53
00:02:05,279 --> 00:02:07,517
A gas is squeezed by a piston.

54
00:02:07,517 --> 00:02:09,063
Is w plus or minus?

55
00:02:12,263 --> 00:02:13,163
Plus!

56
00:02:12,806 --> 00:02:16,601
Work is done on the system,
so energy goes into the bank.

57
00:02:17,251 --> 00:02:20,135
How big is the work, when a gas expands?

58
00:02:20,135 --> 00:02:21,212
Step by step.

59
00:02:21,562 --> 00:02:23,619
The outside pressure is p ex.

60
00:02:23,619 --> 00:02:26,135
It pushes on the piston from outside.

61
00:02:26,885 --> 00:02:30,536
The gas grows from
volume V i to volume V f.

62
00:02:30,536 --> 00:02:32,473
The change is delta V.

63
00:02:33,223 --> 00:02:36,154
Work equals minus p ex times delta V.

64
00:02:36,904 --> 00:02:37,808
Why minus?

65
00:02:37,808 --> 00:02:42,465
When the gas expands, delta V is
plus, but the gas spends energy.

66
00:02:42,465 --> 00:02:44,128
So w comes out minus.

67
00:02:44,878 --> 00:02:49,233
If a gas expands into empty space,
a vacuum, nothing pushes back.

68
00:02:49,233 --> 00:02:51,785
p ex is zero, so the work is zero.

69
00:02:51,785 --> 00:02:53,401
This is free expansion.

70
00:02:54,051 --> 00:02:55,247
Remember this.

71
00:02:55,247 --> 00:02:57,269
Delta U equals q plus w.

72
00:02:57,269 --> 00:02:59,850
Plus always means into the system.

73
00:03:00,550 --> 00:03:02,240
Now, one worked example.

74
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:05,254
A gas takes in three
hundred joules of heat.

75
00:03:05,254 --> 00:03:09,365
It expands from two litres to four
litres, against a steady one bar.

76
00:03:09,765 --> 00:03:13,098
Heat goes in, so q is
plus three hundred joules.

77
00:03:13,848 --> 00:03:17,520
Work is minus one bar,
times four minus two litres.

78
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:19,629
That is minus two litre bar.

79
00:03:20,379 --> 00:03:23,166
One litre bar is one hundred joules.

80
00:03:23,166 --> 00:03:25,782
So w is minus two hundred joules.

81
00:03:26,532 --> 00:03:30,069
Delta U is three hundred,
plus minus two hundred.

82
00:03:30,069 --> 00:03:31,858
Plus one hundred joules.

83
00:03:32,608 --> 00:03:34,647
The gas kept one hundred joules.

84
00:03:34,647 --> 00:03:37,681
It spent the other two
hundred pushing the piston.

85
00:03:38,331 --> 00:03:39,793
Now, the exam trap.

86
00:03:40,143 --> 00:03:43,117
Some books write delta U equals q minus w.

87
00:03:43,117 --> 00:03:44,918
Students mix up the two.

88
00:03:45,318 --> 00:03:50,224
In NCERT, w is work done on the
system, so delta U equals q plus w.

89
00:03:50,224 --> 00:03:52,615
Use one rule all the way through.

90
00:03:53,265 --> 00:03:54,664
Where is this asked?

91
00:03:54,664 --> 00:03:59,105
Expect sign questions, and short
numericals that find delta U, q or w.

92
00:03:59,705 --> 00:04:00,839
Exam level now.

93
00:04:00,839 --> 00:04:05,147
A system gives out one hundred twenty
joules of heat, while two hundred

94
00:04:05,147 --> 00:04:07,185
joules of work is done on it.

95
00:04:07,185 --> 00:04:08,224
Find delta U.

96
00:04:08,224 --> 00:04:09,406
Pause and solve.

97
00:04:14,806 --> 00:04:16,126
The answer is A.

98
00:04:16,126 --> 00:04:17,538
Plus eighty joules.

99
00:04:18,038 --> 00:04:21,332
Heat goes out, so q is
minus one hundred twenty.

100
00:04:21,832 --> 00:04:25,407
Work is done on it, so
w is plus two hundred.

101
00:04:25,907 --> 00:04:28,959
Delta U is minus one
twenty plus two hundred.

102
00:04:28,959 --> 00:04:29,933
Plus eighty.

103
00:04:29,933 --> 00:04:32,412
B is the trap, from flipped signs.

104
00:04:33,012 --> 00:04:34,553
Here is your recap.

105
00:04:34,553 --> 00:04:36,137
Screenshot this card.

106
00:04:39,337 --> 00:04:41,523
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

107
00:04:41,923 --> 00:04:42,823
One.

108
00:04:42,371 --> 00:04:45,584
What are the only two ways
energy can cross a boundary?

109
00:04:46,384 --> 00:04:47,284
Two.

110
00:04:46,794 --> 00:04:49,459
In NCERT, is work done
by a gas plus or minus?

111
00:04:50,259 --> 00:04:51,159
Three.

112
00:04:50,713 --> 00:04:53,442
Why is the work zero when a
gas expands into a vacuum?

113
00:04:54,342 --> 00:04:59,175
Next time: why does a steel pan heat
up faster than the water inside it?

114
00:04:59,175 --> 00:05:01,995
We find out in Enthalpy and Heat Capacity.
